{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "331218950",
    "title": "15-07-2026 Global-e Meeting Notes",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/331218950",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 3,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Meeting Title\n-------------\n\nGlobal-e Integration — Kick-off & Requirements Alignment\n\nDate and Time\n-------------\n\n15 July 2026 — 11:00 AM\n\nAttendees\n---------\n\n| Name | Role / Affiliation |\n| --- | --- |\n| Timothy Boyd | Global-e |\n| Luke Holtfreter | Global-e |\n| Volodymyr Dendevych | Global-e |\n| Sean Doonan | Global-e |\n| Lucy Fu | Zimmermann |\n| Rebecca Jourdan | Zimmermann |\n| Emma Kirwan | Zimmermann |\n| Natasha Lay | Accenture |\n| Charmaine Lew | Accenture |\n| Manikandan Ramachandran | Accenture |\n| Hardi Sempuno | Accenture |\n| Navarro, Marcel Angelo N. | Accenture |\n| victor.t.crisostomo | Accenture |\n\n---\n\nAgenda Items\n------------\n\n### 1. Overview & Architecture Confirmation\n\n* Charmaine opened by demoing the new Zimmermann website.\n* Timothy confirmed Global-e's approach: design is fully controlled by Zimmermann across all pages **except** the Global-e checkout, which is an iframe.\n* Manikandan confirmed the storefront is **fully headless** — no SFRA, PWA Kit only.\n* The checkout flow is triggered via a **Send Cart hook** that passes basket contents to Global-e. The Global-e checkout renders as a **1-page iframe checkout**, which aligns with current designs.\n* Global-e handles: duties & taxes calculation, local payment methods, and the order confirmation screen within the iframe.\n* SFCC still creates the order after Global-e checkout completes (OOTB Global-e cartridge behaviour) — order is then forwarded to NewStore.\n\n### 2. Pricing Strategy\n\n* Two pricing strategies are supported per market (one strategy per country, determined by Zimmermann):\n* **Dynamic pricing** — calculated from a base price; Global-e manages the conversion and applies coefficients. Not real-time but fast. Global-e stores in their database and sends back to SFCC.\n* **Fixed pricing** — fixed pricebook created and maintained in SFCC by Zimmermann. Global-e does **not** need these synced back; they are managed entirely in SFCC.\n* Current implementation is a mix of both dynamic and fixed, market dependent.\n* Timothy confirmed Global-e needs the **full list of countries/storefronts** and **base currencies per site** from Zimmermann.\n* Luke flagged this should not be assumed as a straight lift-and-shift — Zimmermann should confirm whether they want to continue with the same mapping or make adjustments.\n* Natasha raised the importance of understanding existing **Magento limitations** so the team can identify what can be improved in the SFCC implementation.\n\n### 3. Order Flow & Fraud Check\n\n* Global-e performs a **fraud check** before forwarding the confirmed order back to SFCC.\n* **Do not forward to NewStore** until fraud check is passed and order status is updated by Global-e.\n* If the order is fraudulent, Global-e cancels it and SFCC is notified.\n* Global-e sends all **transactional emails** (order confirmation, etc.) — these are not sent until after the fraud check passes.\n* Timothy to share: full order status list and email trigger sequence.\n* Return status updates are posted by Global-e directly to **NewStore** (not SFCC). Manikandan confirmed this is the desired behaviour — the team will rely on NewStore for return status.\n\n### 4. Catalogue Job\n\n* The Global-e cartridge includes a configurable **daily catalogue export job** (batch).\n* Purpose: product classification and tax calculation — Global-e needs to know what products are in the basket.\n* Fields required: **Name, Description, Price, Country of Origin, HS Code**.\n* HS Code: if provided, used as-is. If missing, Global-e can **auto-classify** it.\n* Each site is set up as a **separate account** on the Global-e side, with its own pricebook and base currency — the catalogue job runs per site.\n* Approach: replicate the same site/account structure as current Magento setup.\n\n### 5. Gift Cards\n\n* Global-e confirmed gift card support **is possible** — requires a section in the Global-e checkout for gift card number and PIN.\n* Integration flow: Global-e calls a hook in SFCC → SFCC calls Givex to validate → passes result back to Global-e (with any required format transformation).\n* Emma noted there is an existing limitation between Magento and Global-e for gift cards.\n* **Decision:** Given timelines, gift cards on Global-e storefronts are deferred. Natasha to confirm this sits on the enhancements backlog.\n\n### 6. Sign-in at Checkout / Loyalty\n\n* Global-e checkout **does not currently support sign-in** within the iframe.\n* Use cases for sign-in at checkout: saved addresses, saved cards, loyalty points, customer groups.\n* Current design has sign-in embedded in the checkout page.\n* **Proposed approach:** Two versions of the sign-in flow:\n* **International (Global-e):** Sign in first (pre-checkout), then redirect to Global-e checkout with customer context passed through.\n* **Domestic:** Single-page checkout with sign-in inline (as designed).\n* Rebecca raised this as an **offline action** to work through with the design team.\n* Timothy to check whether Global-e can support login via the SFCC cartridge.\n\n### 7. Catalogue-Based Promotions (VIC / Private Sales)\n\n* Rebecca flagged a known limitation: **catalogue-based promotions** (e.g. whole-catalogue 30% off for VIC customers during private sale events) were historically not supported in Global-e with Magento, and a promo code workaround was used.\n* Timothy believes this **may be supported** in the SFCC cartridge as price calculation works differently in SFCC — will confirm with his SFCC team.\n\n### 8. Scope & Way of Working\n\n* Luke emphasised the need to **lock down scope** — not assume lift-and-shift. Proposed splitting into two tracks: **front-end website** and **back-end fulfilment**.\n* Rebecca confirmed fulfilment flow is unlikely to change significantly — NewStore remains the OMS. A validation session will confirm.\n* Rebecca noted an upcoming **Europe multi-country change** (planned for November) that may impact Global-e scope.\n* Luke flagged Global-e has a broad influence across many epics — Rebecca confirmed the team is aligning on 4 key integration partners (of which Global-e is one) this Friday to prioritise sprint planning accordingly.\n* **Partner forums** to be scheduled — Global-e to be included with relevant team members, avoiding ad hoc calls.\n* Luke confirmed there is a **Trello board with ~9 potential feature enhancements** — to be shared with Global-e to assess feasibility and relevance.\n* Emma requested a **feasibility check** on what is available out of the box.\n* Commercial agreement: Luke confirmed no change to commercials — Global-e will support this implementation under existing terms.\n\n---\n\nAction Items\n------------\n\n| Task | Owner | Due Date | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Share full list of countries/storefronts and base currencies per site | Rebecca Jourdan (Zimmermann) | TBC | Required by Global-e to set up accounts and pricing strategy |\n| Confirm pricing strategy mapping (dynamic vs fixed per country) — lift-and-shift or changes? | Rebecca Jourdan (Zimmermann) | TBC | Should reflect current Magento setup as baseline |\n| Share order status list and transactional email trigger sequence | Timothy Boyd (Global-e) | TBC | Needed to design SFCC order flow and NewStore handoff logic |\n| Share meeting deck/slides | Timothy Boyd (Global-e) | TBC | Referenced during meeting |\n| Confirm gift cards deferred to enhancements backlog | Natasha Lay (Accenture) | TBC | Not in scope for initial go-live |\n| Work through sign-in at checkout flow with design team | Rebecca Jourdan (Zimmermann) / Design team | TBC | Two versions required: international (pre-checkout sign-in) vs domestic (inline) |\n| Check if Global-e SFCC cartridge supports login | Timothy Boyd (Global-e) | TBC | To support loyalty/saved cards/customer group use cases at international checkout |\n| Confirm VIC catalogue-based promotion support in SFCC cartridge | Timothy Boyd (Global-e) | TBC | Historically unsupported in Magento — may work differently in SFCC |\n| Share Trello board of ~9 feature enhancements | Luke Holtfreter (Global-e) | TBC | Global-e to review and assess feasibility/OOTB availability |\n| Schedule detailed technical session (cartridge install, catalogue jobs, BM config) | Global-e / Accenture | TBC | Timothy to lead; SFCC developer to attend |\n| Schedule fulfilment alignment session | Global-e / Accenture / Zimmermann | TBC | Validate NewStore handoff; confirm Europe multi-country change impact |\n| Schedule partner forum cadence | Rebecca Jourdan (Zimmermann) | TBC | Include Global-e; formalise recurring touchpoint |\n\n---\n\nNext Steps\n----------\n\n* Rebecca and the team to align on the 4 key integration partners (including Global-e) this Friday to set sprint priorities.\n* Global-e technical deep-dive sessions to be scheduled: (1) cartridge install/config/catalogue jobs, (2) fulfilment/order flow.\n* Zimmermann to review current Magento/Global-e setup and confirm what should carry forward vs be adjusted for SFCC.\n\n---\n\nOther Notes\n-----------\n\n* Airway Bill (AWB) was referenced in the context of shipping — to be picked up in the fulfilment session.\n* Global-e confirmed scope covers: checkout iframe, duties & taxes, local payment methods, transactional emails, fraud check, order status updates, catalogue export, and returns status posting to NewStore.\n* Each site will have its own Global-e account, pricebook, and base currency — consistent with current Magento structure.",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f4dd",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

