    "content": {
      "value": "Meeting Title\n-------------\n\nAvalara Tax Integration Discussion\n\nDate and Time\n-------------\n\n24 June 2026, 16:00\n\nAttendees\n---------\n\n| Name | Role / Affiliation |\n| --- | --- |\n| Aishwaryawarya Jagtap | Avalara — Solution / Technical Expert |\n| Pankaj VAishwarya | Avalara — Account Manager for Zimmermann |\n| Rebecca Jourdan | Zimmermann |\n| Manikandan Ramachandran | Accenture |\n| Natasha Lay | Zimmermann |\n| Eglantine Emblanc | Zimmermann |\n| Hardi Sempuno | Accenture |\n| Lucy Fu | Zimmermann |\n\n---\n\nAgenda Items\n------------\n\n### 1. Scope of Avalara / AvaTax Integration\n\nZimmermann requires tax calculation via Avalara (AvaTax) across four storefronts:\n\n* **AU** — AvaTax already integrated with Magento; will move to SFCC. Also used to estimate duties for NZ and New Caledonia on the frontend.\n* **US (Domestic)** — AvaTax required for complex state/county/city/special tax calculations.\n* **EU** — AvaTax required to handle different VAT rates across EU member countries.\n* **UK** — AvaTax required to support category-level tax rules (e.g. kids' clothing is zero-rated).\n\nSFCC will integrate **directly** with AvaTax (not via NewStore). NewStore is a separate integration that also uses Avalara for in-store/physical transactions.\n\n### 2. AvaTax SFCC Connector\n\n* Avalara has an existing **SFCC connector/cartridge** that supports tax calculation for US, EU, and UK storefronts.\n* Mani requested the GitHub location / release package for the cartridge — **Aishwarya to follow up**.\n\n### 3. HS Codes vs Avalara Tax Codes\n\nTwo separate concepts were clarified:\n\n* **HS Codes** — Country-specific import codes used for duty calculation (vary per destination country). Zimmermann currently generates these via Avalara's HS code generation service and stores them in AP21 (ERP). Currently held in Magento for AU, used to support NZ duties. Will need to flow into SFCC from AP21.\n* **Avalara Tax Codes** — Global codes maintained by Avalara's team. Used to map products to the correct tax category (e.g. could be used for kids' clothing in the UK). These are separate from HS codes and do not communicate with each other.\n\nKey point: HS codes and Avalara tax codes serve different purposes and are managed independently.\n\n### 4. Product Attribute Mapping in SFCC\n\n* For live tax calculation in SFCC, the product's HS code and/or Avalara tax code need to be available on the order payload sent to AvaTax.\n* HS codes already exist in AP21; if SFCC can pull them from AP21, they can be passed to AvaTax at the time of tax calculation.\n* Eglantine confirmed HS codes are currently uploaded to Avalara for HS code generation, then stored back into AP21.\n* **Open question:** Where exactly do Avalara tax codes (not HS codes) currently live — AP21, Magento, or Avalara itself? RJ suspects the mapping was done directly in Avalara during the NewStore implementation. **RJ/Eglantine to confirm with Simon/IT team.**\n\n### 5. NewStore Avalara Implementation Reference\n\n* Avalara has a note on NewStore/Avalara implemention work, went live December 2025\n* Simon confirmed via RJ that there is a tax mapping in Avalara, but is not across the details.\n* **Eglantine to send an email** explaining how the current NewStore–Avalara setup works, so the team can understand what's already configured and reusable.\n\n### 6. Zimmermann Avalara Test Environment\n\n* A Zimmermann Avalara sandbox environment already exists.\n* **Rebecca to create a user / grant Mani admin access** to the sandbox so development and testing can proceed.\n\n### 7. Tax Commit Timing Best Practice\n\n* Mani asked: when should tax be committed vs. voided in AvaTax (e.g. at cart, checkout, payment)?\n* **Aishwarya to highlight the relevant section in the AvaTax guide**, or send guidance via email.\n* Note: even if a customer does not complete a purchase, a record is created in AvaTax when tax is calculated.\n\n### 8. Returns & Tax Adjustments\n\n* Returns for SFCC are handled via Narvar (outside SFCC).\n* Mani raised whether returns trigger updates in AvaTax. RJ is not certain the current returns process updates AvaTax.\n* For US/Canada, Avalara can prepare tax returns and adjust for product returns — the same order record is updated when returns are filed.\n* **Finance question:** Who is responsible for triggering tax return adjustments in AvaTax? RJ to follow up with finance team.\n\n### 9. EU — Multiple VAT Numbers (One Company)\n\n* Eglantine raised a question: Zimmermann has multiple VAT registrations across EU countries (e.g. France, Italy, Spain) — potentially under different legal entities. Invoices need to be issued under the correct country's VAT number.\n* **Aishwarya confirmed:** AvaTax supports this — when adding your company in AvaTax, you can input different VAT numbers for each country where you have a registration.\n\n---\n\nAction Items\n------------\n\n| Task | Owner | Due Date | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Share GitHub location / release package for AvaTax SFCC cartridge | Aishwarya Jagtap | TBC | Mani needs this to begin development |\n| Send email explaining how current NewStore–Avalara setup works | Eglantine Emblanc | TBC | To help team understand reusable config |\n| Confirm where Avalara tax codes are mapped today (AP21, Magento, or Avalara directly) | Rebecca Jourdan / Eglantine Emblanc | TBC | Involve Simon/IT team |\n| Grant Mani admin access to Zimmermann Avalara sandbox | Rebecca Jourdan | TBC | Sandbox already exists |\n| Send AvaTax best practice guide on tax commit/void timing | Aishwarya Jagtap | TBC | Can highlight relevant section or send via email |\n| Confirm whether current returns process updates AvaTax; determine who triggers tax return adjustments | Rebecca Jourdan | TBC | Finance question — may need separate session |\n| Set up a session with Eglantine, Pankaj/Avalara to go over roadmap | Rebecca Jourdan | TBC |  |\n\n---\n\nNext Steps\n----------\n\n* Pankaj has a meeting with Eglantine and Mark on 25-06-2026 to go over orders / sales order sign-off. Once the sales order is signed, the team can proceed to download and use the Avalara environment.\n* Eglantine and RJ to align with Simon/IT on where Avalara tax codes are currently maintained.\n\n---\n\nOther Notes\n-----------\n\n* The AvaTax Avalara tax code is a **global** code — it does not need to be mapped per country. AvaTax handles the local tax calculation based on the global code plus ship-from / ship-to details.\n* HS codes, by contrast, are **destination-specific** — the same product will have a different HS code depending on which country it is being shipped to.\n* For AU specifically, HS codes are only required to support the NZ storefront duties estimate on the frontend.\n* Any platform (NewStore for in-store, SFCC for online) requires its own direct connection to AvaTara — the mapping done in AvaTax itself is shared, but each platform needs its own integration.",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
